<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tangra</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tangra was the supreme sky god of the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgars">Bulgars</a>, a form of the god Tengri worshipped by many Turkic and Mongol peoples of the Eurasian steppe. Bulgar khans invoked him in inscriptions as the source of their rule. His cult was abandoned after Boris I adopted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> in 864, though elements of steppe belief survived among the nobility for some time.</p></div>
